Unfortunately, Rhino 7 does not provide a built-in support for Python scripting. However, you can use the RhinoCommon API to import a DWG file into Rhino. Here's an example of how you could do this in C#:


```csharp
using Rhino;
using Rhino.DocObjects;
using Rhino.FileIO;

class Example
{
 public static void ImportDwgFile(string fileName)
 {
 RhinoDoc doc = RhinoDoc.ActiveDoc;
 FileReadOptions options = new FileReadOptions();
 options.ImportMode = true;
 int index = doc.Objects.AddFromFile(fileName, options);
 if (index == -1)
 {
 RhinoApp.WriteLine("Failed to import {0}", fileName);
 }
 else
 {
 RhinoApp.WriteLine("Imported {0}", fileName);
 }
 }
}
```
You can use this code as a starting point and modify it to meet your specific needs. For example, you can change the file path, or you can process the imported objects in some way after they have been added to the document.
